It is in an Alphaserver 1000A.  Still an excellent m/c for its age
which has never needed an engineering visit.

The problem was resolved this afternoon from input in the HP resource
forum.  Despite putting the required resolution in the
/var/dt/Xserver.conf this was being overridden by the read only file
resident at /usr/dt/config/Xservers.con  (NB servers not server).  When
this was adjusted - or perhaps removed as a default option although I
didn't test this - the problem goes away and as DBT says, the Permedia
card - although not recognised by the Alpha perhaps due to the SRM not
having a valid handle for it - works perfectly well at 1024x768 and
1280x1024.

This shows the benefit of people helping each other.  I doubt if I
would ever have found this file without help despite knowing a
reasonable amount about Alphas and Tru 64 stretching back to the 3800s
and OSF3.


